    "content": "All 18 checklist items have been executed and recorded — **11 PASS, 7 FAIL**.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Working well:** The core forum loop is solid. Registration, profile editing (bio + comma-separated interests), thread publishing with categories, live replies, single-vote upvote toggles on threads and replies, case-insensitive title/body search with empty-state feedback, category filtering, and both ranking algorithms (Trending by upvotes, Most Active by replies) all behaved correctly — including re-sorting when I manufactured ranking flips with 4 replies on thread-3 and 4 upvotes from 4 distinct accounts on thread-2.\n\n**Failures, roughly by severity:**\n\n1. **CS-17 — Authentication is effectively broken.** Passwords are never checked at sign-in. I logged into `qa.alpha@example.com` with `WrongPassword999` and got a full authenticated session. This is a security defect, not a UX issue.\n\n2. **FT-18 — No persistence layer at all.** A page reload wipes everything: the registered account (valid credentials then rejected), the authored thread (404s), profile edits, replies, and votes all revert to seed state. `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, and cookies are all empty — state is purely in-memory.\n\n3. **CS-22 — Dead end for unauthenticated users.** `/new-thread` while logged out renders a genuinely blank page (empty `body.innerText`, zero hinted elements) rather than a sign-in screen, and the logged-out nav offers no creation entry point at all.\n\n4. **CT-21 / CT-19 / CT-20 — Fabricated numbers.** Category counts (Technology 243 vs 3 real threads) and community stats (1,045 threads vs 9 real) are hard-coded and never update. Reply totals are likewise inflated seed values — thread-1 showed \"24 replies\" while listing 3. And Trending/Most Active state no time window while ranking by lifetime totals, with all four top entries dated \"over 2 years ago.\"\n\n5. **CS-14 — Silent validation.** Empty and whitespace-only thread submissions are correctly blocked, but nothing tells the user why: no error text, and no native constraint validation (`required=false` on both fields, category is a plain `<button>`).\n\nTwo notes worth flagging that didn't change a verdict: duplicate username/email registration is correctly rejected but equally silent, and a just-created account displays \"Joined about 8 hours ago\" — suggesting a timezone offset bug in the relative-date formatting."
  }
